A Cloudflare Worker generated from the Artemis `cf-worker-app` template.

## Develop

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm dev          # wrangler dev — serves http://localhost:8787
```

- `GET /` — hello route
- `GET /healthz` — liveness probe: `200 {"version": "<tag>"}`

## Gates (run before pushing; CI runs them too)

```bash
pnpm lint            # biome ci .
pnpm typecheck       # tsc --noEmit
pnpm test            # vitest run --coverage (coverage floor in vitest.config.ts)
pnpm run test:mutation  # would a test notice if the code were wrong? floor in stryker.config.json
pnpm build           # wrangler dry-run build
```

`test:mutation` is the one worth understanding. Coverage proves a line ran; the mutation
score proves a test would have objected. It rewrites `src/` many ways and fails if too few
of those edits break a test.

**Write acceptance criteria with ids.** In the task packet, number each one
(`- AC-1: an expired token is rejected with a 401`), and claim it from a test by putting
`AC-1:` in the test name. CI then fails for any criterion with no passing test. A criterion
you can only check by hand gets no id — say in the PR how you checked it.

Never lower a coverage or mutation floor to turn a red build green; add the missing test.

CI runs the shared Artemis pipelines (`ci`, `security`, `acceptance`{% if visibility == 'public' %}, `codeql`{% endif %}) on every PR, plus
`mutation`. `scripts/smoke.sh` checks the deployed Worker on every preview and release. The
full standard is the
[testing standard](https://github.com/willzhu16/platform/blob/v1/handbook/testing-standard.md).
See [docs/runbooks/deploy.md](docs/runbooks/deploy.md) and
[docs/runbooks/rollback.md](docs/runbooks/rollback.md) for operations.

